direction: right
title: Sort-Merge Join (SMJ) Architecture

Shuffle: 1. Hash Shuffle Phase {
  style.stroke: "#FBBF24"
  T1: Table 1 (Orders - 2TB)
  T2: Table 2 (Customers - 500GB)
  Net: Cluster Network Hash Shuffle

  T1 -> Net: Hash(key) % 200
  T2 -> Net: Hash(key) % 200
}

Sort: 2. Local Sort Phase {
  style.stroke: "#38BDF8"
  Sort1: Sort Table 1 Keys on Worker
  Sort2: Sort Table 2 Keys on Worker
}

Merge: 3. Sequential Merge Phase {
  style.stroke: "#34D399"
  TwoPointer: Linear Pointer Merge: O(N + M)
  Out: Joined Stream Output
  TwoPointer -> Out
}

Shuffle.Net -> Sort.Sort1: Delivers key partitions { style.stroke: "#38BDF8" }
Shuffle.Net -> Sort.Sort2: Delivers key partitions { style.stroke: "#38BDF8" }
Sort.Sort1 -> Merge.TwoPointer: Sorted stream 1 { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
Sort.Sort2 -> Merge.TwoPointer: Sorted stream 2 { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
